WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:05.740
"I remember, I remember The house
where I was born," A little window.

2
00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.470
The morning sun comes peeping in.

3
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.300
Then the stanza turns to the grown man.

4
00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:15.550
Now, he says, he often wishes
the night had taken him.

5
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.430
And this is Thomas Hood, a poet
famous for comic verse and puns.

6
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.840
A happy memory.

7
00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:24.670
So why would it make him wish he'd died?

8
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.820
In this mission, you'll trace the
pattern that every stanza follows.

9
00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.150
What changes inside each one?

10
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.290
You'll hear its song-like
music: a refrain,

11
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.490
and simple rhymes, almost
like a nursery rhyme.

12
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:42.500
And you'll reach the last stanza,
where fir trees seem to touch the sky.

13
00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:47.230
Your mission: explain why a happy
memory makes him wish he'd died.
